# i.e., each string (except last) ends with "\n\n\n" and last ends with "\n\n"
# 
# This is achievable if: format_section_as_md returns sections separated by additional \n
# For a vector of sections, print! would output them concatenated
# And the last one needs to end with "\n\n"
# 
# One solution: when the apply_md processes a list of sections, it returns ONE string
# that contains all sections formatted with the correct separators:
# - Non-last sections: section_md + "\n" (extra blank before next)
# - Last section: section_md (ends with \n\n already)
# Then the whole thing is one string, printed with print!

# This is the cleanest solution. Let me update apply_md:

