# So "~path/to/file~" -> strikethrough "path/to/file"
# And "~/.config/" (no closing ~) -> ~ as text + "/.config/" as text
# 
# The rule is simple: any ~ (with or without the content being alphanumeric) looks for closing ~
# If closing ~ is found (even with non-alphanumeric content between): strikethrough
# If not found: ~ as text, rest as text (split at the ~ position)
# 
# Now let me implement this in the inline parser.
# I need to add '~' handling similar to '*' and '_'

# Let me update the parse_inline function in markdown.rs to handle ~:
